 White moves the queen, Black captures the rook, winning significant material (5 points). This is a classic knight fork pattern.\n\n**Reason:** The knight on e4 can deliver a devastating royal fork with N: e4-c3, attacking both the white queen and rook simultaneously. White will lose at least the exchange (rook for knight) or more material, giving Black a winning advantage.\n\n**Answer:** N: e4-c3"}
