veloping move because:\n- It develops a piece toward the center\n- It attacks White\'s d4 pawn, putting immediate pressure on White\'s center\n- It prepares castling kingside\n- It keeps maximum flexibility for future plans (can still play e7-e6 or e7-e5)\n- It follows sound opening principles: develop knights before bishops, control the center\n\n**Answer:** N: b8-c6'}
