's center, opens lines for piece development (especially the f8 bishop), and follows classical chess principles. While White has a material advantage with the extra knight, I need to fight for activity and central control. Moves like f6 or h6 to attack the knight would weaken my kingside structure unnecessarily, while e5 improves my position strategically.\n\n**Answer:** P: e7-e5"}
